{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/armv6m/tests/writes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:56.122099Z","id":"14697b00c0f3d2f08793360dd98eb9da08dc1b2b45026d170f8e21f8abb6a209","body":{"detail":"Nothing asserts that an exception frame is marked BY_EXCEPTION (exception.rs:96), that Ethernet DMA marks receive buffers and descriptors BY_DMA (bus.rs:419, 455, 465), that a write stamped equal to `since` is returned (bus.rs:225, 246), or that written_in with a length reaching past the RAM's end, or near u32::MAX, clamps rather than panics (bus.rs:241).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"e7164c125562a602b59a8d80966ac3f406577ce0f30334fc3a2f5b0003e765cb"},"suggested_fix":"Add tests: an SVC from the storing program checks the 8 stacked words' writer; an H7 receive ring fed one frame checks BY_DMA over its buffer; a halted machine's debug_write is found by written_since(now_stamp, 4); written_in(0, 4, last_word, u32::MAX - 8) returns at most one cell.","summary":"The tests cover a CPU store and a probe write but not exception stacking, DMA, the `since` boundary, or reads at a RAM's end","tags":["review","review:memory-visualizer","session:claude-code:27f23ab0-285c-44b4-9dd9-e960c166a6ca"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/armv6m/tests/writes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T12:47:23.193262Z","id":"70d8863f03c347366d6375ee0bcc1faafd17e9a7dd698fb34b020a2714f541e6","body":{"detail":"crates/armv6m/tests/writes.rs (63 lines, 4 tests; `cargo test --release --test writes` -> 4 passed) has no test of BY_EXCEPTION, BY_DMA, a stamp equal to `since` being returned (writes.rs:51 asserts the opposite), or written_in with length past the RAM's end; `grep -rn 'BY_EXCEPTION\\|BY_DMA\\|written_in\\|written_since' crates/armv6m/tests crates/kernel/src` finds no other test use.","kind":"comment","references":"14697b00c0f3d2f08793360dd98eb9da08dc1b2b45026d170f8e21f8abb6a209","summary":"confirmed: writes.rs has four tests covering CPU store, probe write, written_since and written_in only","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:27f23ab0-285c-44b4-9dd9-e960c166a6ca"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/armv6m/tests/writes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:09.504342Z","id":"086be90841959cd06572a54adc4e34a26ecb0187cdfaa34724d68bde9d84dd28","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5f3e6d9","summary":"fixed: crates/armv6m/tests/writes.rs adds an_exception_s_frame_is_the_core_s (SVC frame marked BY_EXCEPTION), a_frame_the_ethernet_dma_receives_is_the_dma_s (buffer and descriptor marked BY_DMA), the since-boundary and standing-still tests, and part_of_a_ram_stops_at_its_end_however_long_it_is_asked_for; 9 passed.","supersedes":"14697b00c0f3d2f08793360dd98eb9da08dc1b2b45026d170f8e21f8abb6a209","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:27f23ab0-285c-44b4-9dd9-e960c166a6ca"]}}
